# Umbrella receipts are append-only: each slice adds exactly one section at the
# end of the file, and `doc-integrity` requires the trunk's copy to stay a byte
# prefix of ours. Git's built-in `union` driver resolves a conflicting hunk by
# concatenating both sides, ours-then-theirs; during a rebase onto main "ours"
# is main, so main's section lands first and the byte-prefix property survives.
# That is exactly the resolution sibling slices were typing out by hand on every
# rebase. The driver cannot tell an append from an edit above the append point —
# `doc-integrity` still enforces that, and a slice still never rewrites text it
# does not own.
receipts/*.md merge=union
